# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/

.DS_store

input/.DS_Store

# chefboost fit() scratch dir (rules.py output + cross-process lock file,
# repair/run_perturbation_repair.py) -- chefboost hardcodes writing to
# <cwd>/outputs/, so we chdir it into this dedicated folder instead of the
# repo root.
.chefboost_scratch/

# --- 2026, GitHub-based code sync (Mac <-> potena01/02/03) ---
# Git repo (chiaragii/repair_with_data) carries CODE ONLY. Everything below is
# either (a) too large for a normal git push (GitHub's hard per-file limit is
# 100MB; road_traffic.xes/hospital_billing.xes alone are 167-177MB) or (b) a
# generated artifact that mining/repair/run_pipeline_*.sh already rebuild
# locally on each server, so shipping it through git would just be dead
# weight and a merge-conflict risk on every run. Raw/cut event logs are
# assumed to already exist on every server (never traveled through git,
# never will).
decision_points/
experiments/*/repair/
experiments.zip
normative_model*.pkl
!evaluation/qualitative/*.pkl
quantitative_evaluation/
*_tree_cache/
n*.log
sepsis_repair.log
results_sepsis.txt
datasets/*_cut/*.xes*
experiments/*/*_cut/*.xes*

# NOTE: pn_normative.pnml is deliberately NOT excluded above (only *.xes* is,
# both under datasets/*_cut/ and under experiments/*/*_cut/) -- unlike
# everything else under datasets/, it can only be produced on a machine with
# a display (ProM's package manager is GUI-only, see
# mining/build_pn_normative.py's docstring), so it DOES need to travel
# through git -- it's also tiny (20-56KB), no size concern.

# vendored third-party lib with its own embedded .git (3rdparty/rulecosi) --
# untouched this session, already present on every server; leaving it out
# avoids git treating it as a broken nested-repo/gitlink entry.
3rdparty/
